oad\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"db6293e6a04f465b131cd3ae8bd5184f6218c3854b3c1e4a584e86f9e64b6e66","event_uuid":"fcc9e9db-2401-48fc-b27f-da26ffef1ec6","position":{"commit_sha":"a774176c6e77dd0ed7a1f6b6d8b8ef2c3a3ec517","position":"1787222786262369720-fcc9e9db-2401-48fc-b27f-da26ffef1ec6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5d12eae74b01ba41ebb9dee66c8c35a6700dcd2745b2332317f9c7447c00e78e","event_uuid":"0fdd5241-297e-4cb3-b8b2-567b391a521a","position":{"commit_sha":"2b4671fbeeb49142608e7e0addfb84c3d65bb5fe","position":"1787223484761882001-0fdd5241-297e-4cb3-b8b2-567b391a521a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787070496032736001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2ecb7193-688c-497f-96b0-96ba7ccbb009","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"b2ff-03f7-a223-4900"},{"link_uuid":"120288aa-a370-4dc7-bb68-71377ffdec11","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b06c-04a9-52b2-42fe"},{"link_uuid":"84d16a83-1778-49d9-9fbb-5df37223bc84","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7550-406f-8635-463d"},{"link_uuid":"24bc83a2-7833-4f81-9150-d9e636742c3c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"cc7f-8723-2f2d-4852"},{"link_uuid":"fcc9e9db-2401-48fc-b27f-da26ffef1ec6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"43d1-8cfd-fc2f-4faa"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAdvanced bridge/reconciler, audit, LLM/review, workflow, identity, and gate commands mix inline argparse construction with manual dispatch. Their current `--help` behavior is also the source of the 21 unsafe/incomplete top-level help forms. The grammar must become reusable without importing optional runtimes.\n\n## Approach\nInventory every registered advanced grammar in `src/rebar/_cli/`, standalone verification/auth command modules, and the reconciler request CLI. For each family:\n\n1. Extract existing argparse construction into the S2a side-effect-free factory contract; migrate manual nested dispatch where required.\n2. Switch the selected runtime handler to the same factory in the same change.\n3. Keep parser factories in lean modules: no Pydantic AI/provider, FastAPI/UI, Jira transport, workflow executor, metrics, tracing, or other optional runtime imports.\n4. Reuse argument-definition helpers between canonical nested bridge forms and `bridge-fsck`, `bridge-probe`, `jira-onboard`, and hidden `bridge-status`; only `prog`, visibility, and replacement epilog differ.\n5. Preserve handler-owned nested command selection, lean modes, backend/mode selection timing, diagnostics, streams, and exit codes. Optional capability enforcement remains S4 and never occurs during parser construction.\n6. Register all parser references and make every visible advanced route generation-ready, without changing top-level help routing yet.\n7. Reconcile the parse-failure seam. The S2a `RebarArgumentParser.error()` raises `ParseError`, not `SystemExit(2)`. Every migrated handler that today translates a parse failure through `except SystemExit` (currently `src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py` and `src/rebar/_commands/trusted_env_cmd.py`) is updated in the same change to also catch `ParseError` and reproduce the identical process exit code (2) and stderr/usage bytes it emits today — no traceback escapes and no exit-code delta.\n8. Preserve bespoke parser presentation. Families that currently pass `usage=`, `formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter`, or `add_help=False` (`verify-opcert`, `verify-commit`, `verify-authorship`, `remote-cert`, `trusted-env`, and the nested bridge parsers) keep those exact behaviors. The S2a factory (`src/rebar/_cli/_parser.py`) is extended additively with optional keyword passthroughs — `usage`, `add_help`, and `formatter_class` (each defaulting to today's S2a behavior, i.e. `RebarHelpFormatter` and `add_help=True`) — so migrated factories request the preserved presentation explicitly while still producing a `RebarArgumentParser` (raises-not-exits) instance. The extension stays stdlib-only and changes no existing call site's behavior.\n\nFamilies include bridge and reconcile, audit, prompt/criteria/LLM setup, review/scan/explain/sign operations, workflow, config/identity verification/trusted-environment/remote-certificate commands, and enrichment.\n\n## Compatibility and Rollback\nNo top-level help cutover occurs here. Current execution behavior remains invariant. The later help normalization is approved, but generated bytes do not become authoritative until S2d. Each family reverts with its handler switch; no stored data changes.\n\n## Testing\nUse parser unit matrices plus real subprocess/interface tests for nested selection, help-safe parser construction, aliases, lean modes, failures, streams, and exit codes. Install import blockers for every heavy optional module and use negative controls that prove selected execution still imports what its mode actually requires.\n\nReadiness proof (AC5): a registry-driven test iterates every advanced route, resolves its recorded parser-factory reference, invokes the factory, and asserts it returns a constructed `argparse.ArgumentParser` bound to the expected `prog` — with heavy optional runtimes import-blocked and without executing any handler — proving each route is deterministically S2d-generation-ready in-session.\n\nParse-failure parity (AC4): production-path tests feed malformed argv to each migrated command through its real entry point and assert the unchanged exit code (2) and stderr/usage bytes, covering the `ParseError`-vs-`SystemExit` seam. Presentation parity: a per-command test asserts `--help`/usage bytes are byte-identical to pre-migration for every command that carried `usage=`/`RawDescriptionHelpFormatter`/`add_help=False`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Every registered advanced command and nested subcommand runtime uses one S2a parser factory; no inline/manual duplicate grammar remains.\n- [x] Canonical and compatibility bridge spellings share argument-definition helpers while retaining approved `prog`, replacement, visibility, and historical usage behavior.\n- [x] Parser construction succeeds in the no-extras environment and imports no handler executor, provider, UI, Jira transport, or other optional runtime.\n- [x] Production-path tests show no unapproved delta in nested selection, accepted/rejected argv, diagnostics, streams, exit codes, help/usage byte output (byte-identical `--help`/usage for commands carrying `usage=`/`RawDescriptionHelpFormatter`/`add_help=False`), or lean-mode availability.\n- [x] Every advanced route has a valid factory reference and is ready for deterministic S2d generation.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/","reason":"Lean advanced/nested command-family parser factories and alias composition helpers."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","reason":"Use shared bridge parser factory and compatibility argument definitions."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py","reason":"Use bridge-setup grammar with historical alias prog."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"Use lean shared parser factories for review/scan/explain/sign commands."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py","reason":"Use lean shared parser factories for prompt/criteria/LLM setup."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_workflow_commands.py","reason":"Use lean shared nested workflow parser factory."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_audit_commands.py","reason":"Use lean shared audit parser factory."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/","reason":"Switch advanced identity/auth/certificate/config handler parsers to shared factories."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/request.py","reason":"Switch reconcile CLI parsing to the shared lean factory."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/","reason":"Advanced real CLI argv, alias, lean-mode, stream, and exit parity."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_advanced_cli_parsers.py","reason":"Pure nested parser and heavy-import exclusion tests."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parser.py","reason":"Additive optional usage/add_help/formatter_class passthroughs so advanced factories preserve bespoke usage/RawDescription/add_help presentation; stays stdlib-only, defaults unchanged."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","b2ff-03f7-a223-4900"],["parent","2635-4aa3-5c14-4b12"],["relates_to","43d1-8cfd-fc2f-4faa"],["relates_to","7550-406f-8635-463d"],["relates_to","b06c-04a9-52b2-42fe"],["relates_to","cc7f-8723-2f2d-4852"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2635-4aa3-5c14-4b12","parent_status_uuid":"3b19a398-a79b-46d8-8f86-d19ad8440a4b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["rp05","cli"],"ticket_id":"a8ce-8ffa-54d7-432f","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-05 S2c — Migrate advanced command grammars to lean argparse factories","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_advanced_cli_parsers.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout.py tests/unit/test_llm_setup_cli.py tests/unit/workflow/test_cli.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC4","dd_text":"Advanced shared-parser, alias, nested, lean-import, and behavior parity"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_advanced_cli_parsers.py -k factory_reference","dd_id":"AC5","dd_text":"All advanced parser references resolve in the base environment"}]},"source_event_uuids":["589a06dd-c316-4f51-a357-8436206820c0","f46ab4e6-383e-42ae-928f-6be9395fbffb","3e480b01-7ba7-42b6-989a-2ba977050ea6","3b19a398-a79b-46d8-8f86-d19ad8440a4b","5cc39033-ad97-48a2-9ff2-1113d920ecbe","377b1c35-dc5d-4f7e-98fd-4bf17a263b2d","120288aa-a370-4dc7-bb68-71377ffdec11","84d16a83-1778-49d9-9fbb-5df37223bc84","24bc83a2-7833-4f81-9150-d9e636742c3c","fcc9e9db-2401-48fc-b27f-da26ffef1ec6","0fdd5241-297e-4cb3-b8b2-567b391a521a"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787227650531623326,"uuid":"c2fd456d-dcb6-4264-84df-28286d81635b"}